Date: Sat, 13 Mar 1993 10:18:19 -0500 (EST)
From: Harry Shapiro <habs@Panix.Com>
Subject: Meta: Ranking System

There is a lot of confusion about the purpose of ranking systems
and how we will implement it/them. (Or if we will).

1) We will not implement a ranking system until it is well tested,
   easy to use, etc.

2) The purpose (the only purpose) for providing rankings is For
   Your Own benefit   A N D   that of other members who also rank.

2b) Rankings will not have any effect on those who subscribe to
   the entire real time list, nor will, in any direct manner,
   the "results" of rankings ever be published to the list.

2c) The set of all Your rankings can be thought of as a "vector"
    pointing to the posts you like and don't like.

2d) The inital way we plan on using the database containing the
    set of all vectors is to compare each members vectors to 
    each others - when their is/are other ranker(s) who have
    a close vector to your own, AND that person(s) likes a post
    you have not ranked, it will be forwarded to you.

3)  Other technology may prove far more useful. The method
    described in item 2 is being used by Carl Feynman to rank
    all science fiction books listed in the Lib. of Congress Catalog.
    This technology should prove successful in this regard.

    It is uncertain if such a technology will prove useful in
    the dynamic fast paced world of the Extropians List.

3a) Other technologies we are planning on implementing will allow
    list members to get or not get posts from specifc users.

    For example, rather than use the ranking system you might
    decide it is better to simply get (and only get) posts from
    Tim May, Perry, Robin, Hal, etc. (You will be forced to, btw,
    get my Meta posts.)

3b) In the real world you will probally want to use a combination
    of these "technologies." (e.g., get messages from certain posters
    but use the ranking system so you don't miss any great posts from
    new list members...)

4)  If you wish to influence (i.e., speed-up) the development of
    this stuff, donations to ExI, explictly directed to the
    "list development fund" will be used to hire/pay for our
     volunter programmer (Ray C.) and others who have agreed to
    help (e.g., Derek).

    If you wish to stop this process send ray money directly,
    asking him to use your payment to have a "good time" and
    forget about list development.

